# WynlandOS: programs that may have writable+executable memory (W^X off
# for them). JIT compilers that write their code in place need it: V8 in
# Node.js (and later Chromium, Electron). One absolute path per line, as
# the program is started; read by the kernel at every execve
# (kernel/elf.c, jit_listed()). Everything else keeps W^X, unless it is
# started with WYNLAND_ALLOW_JIT=1.
/usr/bin/node
/usr/bin/nodejs
